  "$comment": "Example routing snapshot, not a live availability catalog. Work names an intelligence tier; the standalone router picks the route. Scores are Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index values (snapshot 2026-10-16); free-model scores live in scores.json. Machine 'routing' overrides this policy, then project 'routing' overrides that ('routes' replaces, 'routes_extra' appends). T3 selects providers separately through its capability tools.",
  "tiers": {
    "bulk":        { "floor": 20, "fallback_floor": 15, "writes_code": false, "use_for": "Mechanical lookup, classification, extraction" },
    "research":    { "floor": 30, "fallback_floor": 26, "writes_code": false, "use_for": "Retrieval, summaries, reports, documentation drafts" },
    "code-simple": { "floor": 40, "fallback_floor": 38, "writes_code": true,  "use_for": "Scaffolding, config, simple edits, small tests" },
    "code":        { "floor": 42, "fallback_floor": 40, "writes_code": true,  "use_for": "Everyday features and refactors" },
    "code-hard":   { "floor": 48, "fallback_floor": 42, "writes_code": true,  "use_for": "Multi-file features, parsers, debugging, reviews" },
    "frontier":    { "floor": 50, "fallback_floor": 48, "writes_code": true,  "use_for": "Reverse engineering, binary formats, architecture" }
  },
  "$frontier_comment": "Subscription routes carry Artificial Analysis's snapshot measures (2026-10-27): cost_per_task (USD at API prices), index_tokens_m (output tokens, millions), output_speed (tokens per second). Tiers rank each family's Pareto frontier; a pin reaches any route. Configure model IDs, supported efforts, scores, and routing preferences for the actual deployment.",
  "$pin_only_comment": "Example effort policy: only explicit pins reach max, and gate reviews and re-evaluations exclude it. Override pin_only_efforts in machine or project routing when needed.",
